+# Block table of the DFlash2 draft-private pruned LM head (litos patch 4001-draft-pruned-head).
+#
+# The draft proposes only from DRAFT_HEAD_BLOCKS_N whole 128-id blocks of the target vocabulary: the
+# first DRAFT_HEAD_BLOCKS_N entries of DRAFT_HEAD_BLOCK_ORDER. EXL3 rotates the head's outputs in
+# 128-column Hadamard groups, so an aligned 128-column block slices exactly out of the quantized
+# trellis (trellis[:, 8b:8b+8], svh[128b:128b+128]); single ids cannot.
+#
+# Ranking recipe (offline, general text only; no benchmark prompt or answer is read):
+#   1. Forced, first and in id order: blocks 0..127 (ids 0..16383, the lowest BPE merge
+#      ranks) and every block holding an added/special/control token (ids 248044..248076:
+#      blocks 1937, 1938).
+#   2. Then blocks by token mass in a general local corpus (Python stdlib, man pages, system docs,
+#      sympy/mpmath/networkx/numpy sources; the four families weighted equally), ties to the lower
+#      block index. Tokenizer: Qwen3.5/3.6/3.8 family (vocab 248320).
+# Only this vocabulary has a table; any other target vocabulary keeps the full head.
+#
+# Committed tokens are always the target's greedy verify argmax, so pruning changes only which
+# proposals are made (acceptance), never which token a verified position commits.
+
